          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The World Soul</strong><br>\nFollowing the Divine Intellect is the World Soul, which links the material world to the spiritual realm. The World Soul, according to Plotinus, is responsible for the life and order we see in the physical universe. It animates all living things and maintains harmony, reflecting the order of the cosmos.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Material World and Sensation</strong><br>\nPlotinus considered the material world as a diluted version of the spiritual. He posited that our sensory experiences and the physical realm are far removed from the perfection of The One. He urged people to look beyond the material world to understand the spiritual truth of existence.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Path to The One</strong><br>\nFor Plotinus, the ultimate goal of life was to achieve a mystical union with The One through the intellect and the purification of the soul. This union could only be reached through philosophical reasoning, self-discipline, and inner contemplation. Plotinus emphasized that this journey was an inward one, as The One lies beyond the physical and intellectual realms.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
